<content>
  <section><para>In this lesson, you will not only write equations given a point and slope or two points but also from verbal descriptions and from tables.</para>
<para>When you finish this lesson, you will be able to:</para>
<list>
  <item> Write equations from a point and slope. </item>
  <item> Write equations from two points. </item>
  <item> Write equations from a verbal description. </item>
  <item> Write equations from a table. </item>
</list>

<para>Here are the <emphasis>activities</emphasis> that will help you reach those goals:</para>
<list>
  <item> 1.13.1: Writing Linear Equations </item>
  <item> 1.13.2: Creating Tables from Verbal Descriptions </item>
  <list>
    <item> 1.13.2: Self Check </item>
    <item> 1.13.2: Additional Resources </item>
  </list>
  <item> 1.13.3: Matching Tables, Equations, and Graphs </item>
  <list>
    <item> 1.13.3: Self Check </item>
    <item> 1.13.3: Additional Resources </item>
  </list>
  <item> 1.13.4: Creating a Table from an Equation </item>
</list>
<para>After that, you’ll <emphasis>practice and review</emphasis>.</para>
<list>
  <item> 1.13.5: Practice </item>
  <item> 1.13.6: Lesson Summary </item>
</list>
</section>
</content>
